[I] Extremely lightweight compatibility layer between dataframe libraries

[T] Narwhals is an extremely lightweight and extensible Python compatibility
[T] layer between dataframe libraries. It offers a subset of the Polars API
[T] with full support for pandas, Polars, PyArrow, cuDF and Modin and lazy
[T] support for Dask, DuckDB, PySpark and others, without adding
[T] dependencies.

[U] https://github.com/narwhals-dev/narwhals

